# [DD-13b.W23.3] S-R2's REFUSING half: `adaptation` is REQUIRED when
# `fidelity` is not `verbatim` (format_design §2.14 rule 3), and the
# schema row carries that as `required-if fidelity != verbatim` rather
# than as parser code — so a plant that DROPS the clause makes this file
# accepted while its twin stays accepted, and only the pair can tell the
# rule from its absence.
#
# CLASS `schema-constraint`: the line attached correctly, the record's
# own kinds are all legal, and what failed is a DECLARED rule over the
# scope. The refusal points at the record rather than at a line, because
# there is no offending line — the offence is one that is missing.
#
# The condition names a SIBLING, which is why the whole record has to be
# read before it can be answered: `fidelity` may be written above or
# below `adaptation`, and leg A evaluates every scope-ranging constraint
# when the frame CLOSES for exactly that reason.
pattern a+
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-15
  license MIT
  fidelity adapted
m "aaa" 0 3
